OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Mon 9 Nov to Wed 18 Nov
OL,6,FHigh pressure begins to migrate away
OL,7,Fto the east allowing frontal systems
OL,8,Fto attempt to progress into the UK
OL,9,Ffrom the southwest, although exactly
OL,10,Fhow much progress into the UK this
OL,11,Fmakes is uncertain. However there is a
OL,12,Fgreater chance that at least the
OL,13,Fsouthern half of the UK will see a
OL,14,Fchange to milder and wetter
OL,15,Fconditions, at least for a time, while
OL,16,Fthe north is more likely to remain
OL,17,Fdrier. Toward the end of next week we
OL,18,Fmay start to see some colder
OL,19,Fconditions spread from the north to
OL,20,Fmuch of, if not all of the UK, but
OL,21,Fwhile the nature of this colder
OL,22,Foutbreak is very uncertain , it could
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fbring some wintry showers to the
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fnorthern UK briefly, with the south
OL,25,Ftrending drier once again.
